---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SankeyExplorer from '../components/SankeyExplorer.astro';
import {roots,titles} from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="Home">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Chicago public money, one flow at a time</p>
    <h1>Where does the money go?</h1>
    <p class="lede">Explore the City, public schools and parks budgets. Each is a separate budget, not part of a combined total. Select a flow to see the boxes inside and where its numbers come from.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-label="Explore budget flows">
    <SankeyExplorer />
  </section>
  <section class="hero" aria-labelledby="more-ways">
    <h2 id="more-ways">More ways to explore</h2>
    <form action="/find" role="search">
      <label for="home-search">Find a school, park, department or box</label>
      <div><input class="search-field" id="home-search" name="q" type="search" placeholder="Try police, parks or a school"/><button type="submit">Find</button></div>
    </form>
    <p>Prefer a list? Browse the detailed budget pages: {roots.map((root,index)=><>{index>0?' · ':''}<a href={`/${root}`}>{titles[root]}</a></>)}.</p>
    <h2>How to read this</h2>
    <p>Some numbers are printed in the budget. Others are estimates, leftovers or money paid so far. Their labels tell you which is which.</p>
    <p><a href="/glossary">Learn the words</a> · <a href="/about">How we built this</a> · <a href="/gaps">What we could not find</a></p>
  </section>
</Base>
